  "concept": "วันอาสาฬหบูชา",
  "rationale": "Magenta-สังฆทาน;The reason why Buddhists like to make merit by giving offerings to the Sangha comes from the Dakkhinavibhanga Sutta [ 1 ] in the Tripitaka, which contains content related to offerings to the Sangha as follows (in brief):\n\n\"When the Lord Buddha was still alive, he was staying at the Nigrodharam Monastery in Kapilavastu. Queen Mahapajapati Gotami, the Lord Buddha 's maternal aunt, had a strong faith and wove a robe herself to offer to the Lord Buddha. However, the Lord Buddha refused to accept the robe and told Queen Mahapajapati Gotami to offer it to the central Sangha because he believed that offering the robe as a Sangha offering would bring more merit than offering it to the Lord Buddha, the Supreme Teacher. (Offering or giving alms to the Lord Buddha, monks, or ordinary people is considered a form of patipuklika offering.) Furthermore, offering it as a Sangha offering is considered a form of worship of the Lord Buddha, the leader of all Sangha.",
  "source": "https://fth0.com/uppic/12100705/activity/12100705_0_20210721-213849.jpg",
  "reference": "https://th.wikipedia.org/wiki/สังฆทาน"
